    "answer": "⚡ **Newton's Second Law of Motion:**\n\nThe net force acting on an object equals the rate of change of its linear momentum. For constant mass:\n$$\\mathbf{F = m \\cdot a}$$\n• $F$ = Net Force (Newtons, N)\n• $m$ = Mass (kg)\n• $a$ = Acceleration ($m/s^2$)",
