    "answer": "🌿 **Photosynthesis Explained:**\n\nPlants convert sunlight, carbon dioxide, and water into chemical glucose energy while releasing oxygen into the atmosphere:\n$$\\mathbf{6CO_2 + 6H_2O + \\text{Sunlight} \\rightarrow C_6H_{12}O_6 + 6O_2}$$\n• **Light-Dependent Reactions:** Occur in thylakoid membranes, splitting $H_2O$ and generating ATP and NADPH.\n• **Calvin Cycle (Light-Independent):** Occurs in the stroma, using ATP and NADPH to fix $CO_2$ into glucose sugar.",
